 "assessment": {
  "original_metric_verdict": "NOT defensible as originally framed. '866-389-2727 = the plan's own call center' is false; it is the provider organization's (CVS MinuteClinic's) national booking line and matches the org's NPPES record. Publishing 'X% of providers have only the plan's call-center number' for CareSource would be a factual error.",
  "sampling_artifact": "the 1,598-per-1,000-records figure from the first probe counted phone occurrences per ADDRESS; multi-address MinuteClinic records (up to 134 addresses) inflated it. Record-level truth in WI: 657/19,956 = 3.3% only-this-number, 842/19,956 = 4.2% list it anywhere.",
  "defensible_reframe_1": "phone-concentration metric: share of records whose ONLY listed phone is a number shared by >=N other records, published WITH attribution of the number's owner (plan call center vs provider-org central line vs unknown). Central lines like MinuteClinic's or Kaiser's are a lower-severity class than a plan-owned call center.",
  "defensible_reframe_2": "geographic-relevance flag (the stronger finding here): 809 of 842 cohort records (96.1%) have no Wisconsin service address at all; 237 cohort records include Georgia addresses and 903 of the cohort's 2,621 address rows are in Georgia. Whole file: 1,792 records (9.0%) in the WI QHP file have zero Wisconsin addresses. Fair framing: 'the payer's own published Wisconsin file lists N providers whose service addresses are all outside Wisconsin'.",
  "bh_relevance": "none of the affected records match behavioral-health specialties in any of the 4 states; this flag does not support the mental-health narrative and should not be presented as such."
 }
